---
<BaseLayout title="Construction Estimating & Job Costing Excel Toolkit PRO" description="Estimate and quote in one Excel workbook; track actual costs, remaining costs and job profit in another. Complete Toolkit PRO v3.2 package: US$19.99." schema={schema}>
<Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:"Mercer Lane Construction Estimating & Job Costing Toolkit PRO"}]}/>

<header class="page-head wrap">
<p class="eyebrow">TOOLKIT PRO · VERSION 3.2 · MICROSOFT EXCEL</p>
<h1>Construction Estimating &amp; Job Costing Toolkit PRO</h1>
<p class="lede">Build a quote you can review. Track what the accepted job actually costs. Keep estimating and job control in two focused Excel workbooks.</p>
<div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://buy.stripe.com/00wfZj3M9fKt5A62JSds400" data-pro-checkout>Get the complete toolkit — US$19.99</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#included">See what you receive</a></div>
<p class="byline">One-time digital purchase. US$19.99 plus applicable tax. Secure ZIP download after successful payment. Microsoft Excel desktop required.</p>
</header>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>Two workbooks. Two clear jobs.</h2><div class="grid-2">
<article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">01 · BEFORE THE JOB</p><h3>Estimate &amp; Quote Builder</h3><p>Save a separate file for each estimate. Work from project setup and scope through takeoff, materials, labour, subcontract quotes, equipment and other costs, company recovery, markup or margin and bid review.</p><p>Readiness checks highlight unresolved issues before you release a Classic, Modern or Compact customer proposal. The Estimate Overview chart helps you see the cost build-up.</p><p><strong>27 sheets</strong>, including a values-only Job Handoff for accepted work.</p></article>
<article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">02 · AFTER ACCEPTANCE</p><h3>Job Cost &amp; Profit Control</h3><p>Keep one working master for the business. Register accepted jobs, record expenses and labour, track subcontract commitments and approved changes, and review invoices and cash received.</p><p>Enter remaining costs to see a forecast final result. Review budget against actual and forecast costs, contribution after company recovery, portfolio status and lessons for future estimates.</p><p><strong>14 sheets</strong>, with a Dashboard, Job Review and Portfolio. Three editable Excel dashboard charts make comparisons easier to see.</p></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><h2>See the job-control dashboard</h2><p>The completed fictional Oakridge example shows the dashboard populated. Your own results depend on the costs, approved changes and remaining-cost review you enter.</p><img src="/images/construction-toolkit/v32-dashboard.png" alt="Populated Job Cost and Profit Control dashboard in the fictional Oakridge example" loading="lazy" width="1200" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--line)"/><p class="byline">Example data for training. Figures are not recommended prices, rates or business targets.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint" id="included"><div class="wrap"><h2>The complete US$19.99 package</h2><div class="grid-3">
<article class="card"><h3>Two clean core workbooks</h3><p>Estimate &amp; Quote Builder and Job Cost &amp; Profit Control, ready for your own inputs. Formula cells are protected against routine accidental overwrite.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Two separate worked demos</h3><p>Estimate Demo and Job Cost Demo show the fictional Oakridge workflow in each tool. Start your own work from the clean files.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Five bonus workbooks</h3><p>Quick Estimate, True Labour Cost, Overhead Recovery, Markup &amp; Margin, and Change Order Pricing.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Three proposal layouts</h3><p>Classic, Modern and Compact layouts use the reviewed estimate, keeping internal labour, overhead and margin calculations out of client-facing output.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Editable and printable forms</h3><p>Project information, supplier and subcontractor quote requests, post-job review, and printable scope, takeoff, pre-estimate, bid-review and job-cost sheets.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Guides and worked examples</h3><p>Start Here, first-10-minutes and first-estimate workflows, the full user guide, worked bid examples, proposal examples, licence and version information.</p></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><h2>From an accepted quote to job control</h2><ol><li><strong>Build and review the estimate.</strong> Save a job-specific copy of Estimate &amp; Quote Builder and resolve the readiness checks before issuing the proposal.</li><li><strong>Capture the accepted baseline.</strong> Complete Job Handoff after acceptance. Copy its row as values into Add New Job in your business Job Cost &amp; Profit Control master, then register the prepared row as values.</li><li><strong>Record the work.</strong> Enter job expenses, labour, subcontract records, approved changes, invoices and cash received.</li><li><strong>Review the expected finish.</strong> Review remaining costs and company recovery, update the review date and check Dashboard, Job Review and Portfolio.</li></ol><p>The files have no external workbook links or macros. The handoff is a deliberate copy-and-paste-values step; later estimate changes do not silently alter the registered baseline.</p><h2>Capacity and compatibility</h2><p>The supplied job-costing master holds up to <strong>30 registered jobs</strong>. Main transaction logs have 300 entry rows each; subcontract and learning logs have 150 rows each. Keep backups and monitor capacity as your records grow.</p><p>Use modern <strong>Microsoft Excel desktop</strong>. Google Sheets and Excel Online are not claimed as supported. Use Excel's normal print or Save PDF controls for client proposals.</p><h2>What the figures tell you</h2><p>Gross profit is revenue less direct job costs. Contribution after company recovery also deducts the company overhead allocation you enter. Forecast profit includes expected remaining costs. Profit and cash received answer different questions.</p><p>The toolkit supports estimating and job reviews. It does not replace accounting software, prescribe your rates or commercial targets, or guarantee profit or estimate accuracy.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>Try the free tool first</h2><div class="grid-2"><article class="card"><h3>Construction Job Profit Calculator</h3><p>Check one job's revenue, costs, gross profit, contribution, margin and markup. Compare estimated against actual or forecast figures in the browser.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="/tools/construction-job-profit-calculator/">Calculate one job free</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Understand construction job costing</h3><p>Learn how an accepted estimate, actual costs and a remaining-cost forecast fit together before choosing a workbook.</p><a class="text-link" href="/construction-job-costing/">Read the job-costing guide →</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow prose"><h2>Before you buy</h2><h3>Is this a subscription?</h3><p>No. The complete v3.2 package is a one-time purchase for US$19.99 plus applicable tax.</p><h3>Do I get both core workbooks?</h3><p>Yes. Both clean core workbooks, both worked demos, five bonuses, forms and documentation are included.</p><h3>Does the dashboard update automatically?</h3><p>The workbook calculates from your recorded inputs. Enter actual costs and approved changes, review remaining costs and company recovery, and update the review date so the forecast reflects your latest review.</p><h3>Can I import transactions from accounting software?</h3><p>No automatic accounting integration is included. Enter records into the provided logs and follow the guide's values-only handoff.</p><h3>How do I receive the files?</h3><p>Successful Stripe checkout redirects you to a secure download page. Save the ZIP and extract it before opening the workbooks. There is no physical product.</p><h3>What if I need help or have a refund question?</h3><p>See <a href="/digital-products/">digital delivery, compatibility and refund information</a>. Contact Mercer Lane Press using the email address used at checkout if you cannot access a paid download.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>Build estimates. Control accepted jobs.</h2><p>Get the complete Construction Estimating &amp; Job Costing Toolkit PRO v3.2 for <strong>US$19.99</strong>, plus applicable tax.</p><a class="button" href="https://buy.stripe.com/00wfZj3M9fKt5A62JSds400" data-pro-checkout>Get the complete toolkit — US$19.99</a><p class="byline">Check <a href="/digital-products/">digital-product information</a> and <a href="/terms/">site terms</a> before purchase. The product licence is included with the download.</p></div></section>
